    // X.5 NOTE
    "_X5": "─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────",
    "_X5_tag": "X.5 NOTE — Final Anchor [NOTE]",
    "_X5_note": "Demo-test is Day 5 energy — the waters bringing forth abundantly. Genesis 1:20-21: 'Let the waters bring forth abundantly the moving creature that hath life.' Not creating the water (bare-bone did that — Days 1-3). Not filling the earth (library did that — Day 3). Not governing with lights (executable did that — Day 4). Day 5 is ABUNDANCE — the waters teeming with life. Demo-test is that abundance: 9 test categories proving the type works from every angle. ConstructorTests, BuilderTests, TransitionTests, QueryTests, IdentityTests, ErrorTests, EdgeCaseTests, TableDrivenTests, IntegrationTests — each category is a species of verification, each test is a creature bringing the crate to LIFE through proof. The waters were bounded on Day 2. The land appeared on Day 3. Library grew from the land. Executable governed like the lights. But demo-test TEEMS — abundantly, moving, alive. When a test passes, it says: 'this works.' When all tests pass, they say: 'this LIVES.' The concern_coverage ordering is the ecosystem — from construction (birth) through integration (community). Every test is accountability. Every assertion is truth-telling. The abundance is not excess — it is THOROUGH WITNESS to the code's correctness.",
    "_X5_scripture": "And God said, Let the waters bring forth abundantly the moving creature that hath life, and fowl that may fly above the earth in the open firmament of heaven. And God created great whales, and every living creature that moveth, which the waters brought forth abundantly, after their kind. — Genesis 1:20-21",
    "_X5_anchor": "Demo-test is abundant verification. The waters teem. Every test is a creature proving the code lives. Accountability through abundance.",

